# Manual exercise of POST /api/schedules/optimize (docs/api-contract.md section 6.4).
# Open in VS Code with the REST Client extension, or JetBrains' HTTP client,
# and click "Send Request" above each block in order.
#
# Most requests send explicit prices in "forecast", so they never expire: the
# optimiser prices everything from the request, whatever today's date is.
# Request 6 uses "forecastLocation" instead, which reads the stored forecast
# (or the history-based fallback curve when none covers the window).

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Log in. Uses the auto-created, pre-verified admin account from
### DataInitializer, which skips the email OTP step.
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "admin@datacenter.io",
    "password": "Admin@2026!"
}

###
@token = {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2. The contract's worked example. Expect 200, status SCHEDULED,
### provenOptimal true. The job moves from 10:00 ($112) to 01:00 the next day
### ($24): baselineCostUsd 1.0752, optimizedCostUsd 0.2304, savings 0.8448
### (78.57%), perJobStatus OPTIMISED, one allocation at 2026-10-21T01:00:00Z.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/schedules/optimize
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "jobs": [
    {
      "id": 101,
      "name": "LLM Fine-Tuning Run #42",
      "cpuHours": 64.0,
      "gpuHours": 16.0,
      "originalStartTime": "2026-10-20T10:00:00Z",
      "deadline": "2026-10-21T18:00:00Z",
      "flexibilityWindowHours": 15,
      "isExempt": false
    }
  ],
  "forecast": [
    { "intervalStartUtc": "2026-10-20T10:00:00Z", "predictedPrice": 112.0 },
    { "intervalStartUtc": "2026-10-20T11:00:00Z", "predictedPrice": 100.0 },
    { "intervalStartUtc": "2026-10-21T01:00:00Z", "predictedPrice": 24.0 }
  ]
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3. A job spread over several hours. 600 CPU-hours needs at least three
### hours at 256 per hour; it may start at 10:00 or 11:00 and must finish by
### 16:00; 13:00 is down to 100 CPU-hours. Expect 200 with a start at 11:00 and
### consecutive allocations: tiny shares at 11:00 and 12:00 (a run cannot skip
### hours), then 100 CPU-hours at 13:00, 256 at 14:00 and the rest at 15:00.
### The allocations' cpuHours add up to 600.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/schedules/optimize
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "jobs": [
    {"id": 201, "name": "Large batch", "cpuHours": 600.0, "gpuHours": 0.0,
     "originalStartTime": "2026-10-20T10:00:00Z", "deadline": "2026-10-20T16:00:00Z",
     "flexibilityWindowHours": 1, "isExempt": false}
  ],
  "forecast": [
    { "intervalStartUtc": "2026-10-20T10:00:00Z", "predictedPrice": 60.0 },
    { "intervalStartUtc": "2026-10-20T11:00:00Z", "predictedPrice": 55.0 },
    { "intervalStartUtc": "2026-10-20T12:00:00Z", "predictedPrice": 40.0 },
    { "intervalStartUtc": "2026-10-20T13:00:00Z", "predictedPrice": 15.0 },
    { "intervalStartUtc": "2026-10-20T14:00:00Z", "predictedPrice": 18.0 },
    { "intervalStartUtc": "2026-10-20T15:00:00Z", "predictedPrice": 20.0 }
  ],
  "capacityOverrides": [
    { "intervalStartUtc": "2026-10-20T13:00:00Z", "maxCpuHours": 100.0, "maxGpuHours": 64.0 }
  ]
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 4. A job with no room (AC5). The exempt job fills 10:00 and the other job may
### only run at 10:00. Expect 200 (NOT an error), status NEEDS_ATTENTION; the
### second item is NO_FEASIBLE_SLOT with null times, no allocations, null costs,
### a reason, and is left out of the totals.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/schedules/optimize
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "jobs": [
    {"id": 301, "name": "Exempt, fills the hour", "cpuHours": 256.0, "gpuHours": 0.0,
     "originalStartTime": "2026-10-20T10:00:00Z", "deadline": "2026-10-20T11:00:00Z",
     "flexibilityWindowHours": 0, "isExempt": true},
    {"id": 302, "name": "No room left", "cpuHours": 100.0, "gpuHours": 0.0,
     "originalStartTime": "2026-10-20T10:00:00Z", "deadline": "2026-10-20T11:00:00Z",
     "flexibilityWindowHours": 0, "isExempt": false}
  ],
  "forecast": [ { "intervalStartUtc": "2026-10-20T10:00:00Z", "predictedPrice": 10.0 } ]
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 5. Negative savings. Each job alone would run at 10:00 ($20), but only 300
### CPU-hours fit there, so 100 CPU-hours of work has to use 11:00 ($50). Expect
### 200, baselineCostUsd 0.4, optimizedCostUsd 0.55, projectedSavingsUsd -0.15
### (-37.5%), and an explanation saying why.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/schedules/optimize
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "jobs": [
    {"id": 401, "name": "Contender A", "cpuHours": 200.0, "gpuHours": 0.0,
     "originalStartTime": "2026-10-20T10:00:00Z", "deadline": "2026-10-20T12:00:00Z",
     "flexibilityWindowHours": 1, "isExempt": false},
    {"id": 402, "name": "Contender B", "cpuHours": 200.0, "gpuHours": 0.0,
     "originalStartTime": "2026-10-20T10:00:00Z", "deadline": "2026-10-20T12:00:00Z",
     "flexibilityWindowHours": 1, "isExempt": false}
  ],
  "forecast": [
    { "intervalStartUtc": "2026-10-20T10:00:00Z", "predictedPrice": 20.0 },
    { "intervalStartUtc": "2026-10-20T11:00:00Z", "predictedPrice": 50.0 }
  ],
  "clusterCapacity": { "maxConcurrentCpuHours": 300.0, "maxConcurrentGpuHours": 64.0 }
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 6. Prices from the stored forecast for a location. Prices load from the
### earliest originalStartTime for horizonHours. Without stored forecasts for
### that window, usedSeededFallbackPrices is true and the explanation says so.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/schedules/optimize
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "jobs": [
    {"id": 501, "name": "Overnight training", "cpuHours": 1500.0, "gpuHours": 150.0,
     "originalStartTime": "2026-10-20T17:00:00Z", "deadline": "2026-10-21T20:00:00Z",
     "flexibilityWindowHours": 10, "isExempt": false}
  ],
  "forecastLocation": "LZ_NORTH",
  "horizonHours": 48
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 7. Error cases. Each returns success false, a message naming the problem,
### and no data - never a partial schedule.

### Expect 400: jobs is required
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/schedules/optimize
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "forecastLocation": "LZ_NORTH" }

### Expect 400: deadline before originalStartTime
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/schedules/optimize
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "jobs": [
    {"id": 1, "name": "bad", "cpuHours": 10.0, "gpuHours": 0.0,
     "originalStartTime": "2026-10-20T14:00:00Z", "deadline": "2026-10-20T09:00:00Z",
     "flexibilityWindowHours": 0, "isExempt": false}
  ],
  "forecast": [ { "intervalStartUtc": "2026-10-20T14:00:00Z", "predictedPrice": 10.0 } ]
}

### Expect 400: cannot finish by its deadline even alone on the cluster
### (100 CPU-hours needs a full hour; the deadline leaves 30 minutes)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/schedules/optimize
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "jobs": [
    {"id": 1, "name": "Impossible deadline", "cpuHours": 100.0, "gpuHours": 0.0,
     "originalStartTime": "2026-10-20T14:00:00Z", "deadline": "2026-10-20T14:30:00Z",
     "flexibilityWindowHours": 6, "isExempt": false}
  ],
  "forecast": [ { "intervalStartUtc": "2026-10-20T14:00:00Z", "predictedPrice": 10.0 } ]
}

### Expect 400: start time not on the hour
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/schedules/optimize
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "jobs": [
    {"id": 1, "name": "bad", "cpuHours": 10.0, "gpuHours": 0.0,
     "originalStartTime": "2026-10-20T14:30:00Z", "deadline": "2026-10-20T18:00:00Z",
     "flexibilityWindowHours": 0, "isExempt": false}
  ],
  "forecast": [ { "intervalStartUtc": "2026-10-20T14:00:00Z", "predictedPrice": 10.0 } ]
}

### Expect 422: the job's original hour has no price, so its baseline cannot be priced
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/schedules/optimize
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "jobs": [
    {"id": 1, "name": "unpriced", "cpuHours": 10.0, "gpuHours": 0.0,
     "originalStartTime": "2026-10-20T14:00:00Z", "deadline": "2026-10-20T18:00:00Z",
     "flexibilityWindowHours": 2, "isExempt": false}
  ],
  "forecast": [ { "intervalStartUtc": "2026-10-20T15:00:00Z", "predictedPrice": 10.0 } ]
}

### Expect 403: no token
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/schedules/optimize
Content-Type: application/json

{"jobs": []}
